1. What the simulation is, and is not

Port Alder is a simulation. "Sentient" is a design word, not a claim of
consciousness: every agent carries needs, a mood, a personality, memories
and expectations, updates them from what happens to it, and decides from
them.

Port Alder is modelled on Everett, Washington, and on the county, state
and nation around it. Its citizens, households, businesses, banks and
officials are invented. Any resemblance to a real person or business is
coincidence. A Social Information Number is not a Social Security number
and identifies no real person.


2. Laws, rules and figures

The simulation restates tax, payroll, benefit, housing and other rules of
the United States and of Washington State, and published figures such as
populations, wages, rents and rates, as they stood when it was written.
They are quoted for the simulation's purposes and are not warranted. Check
them against the primary sources (src/rules.js and src/periphery.js name
them) before relying on them. Nothing here is legal, tax, financial,
medical, engineering or safety advice.


